# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile, which is the repo root.
#
# node_modules is the important line: the image installs its own with pnpm, and
# shipping the host's would both bloat the context and carry linux-x64 binaries
# built against a different libc than the one in the image.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets. The container is configured entirely through compose's env_file, and
# `pnpm start` passes --env-file-if-exists, so a copied .env would silently win.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and caches — nothing here is used by the image.
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.vite
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.oxlintcache
**/.prettiercache

# The frontend is built on the host and deployed as static files, so none of it
# belongs in the image — except its manifest. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# compares the lockfile against every workspace manifest before it decides the
# lockfile is current, so a missing apps/web/package.json fails the install even
# though nothing in the image imports it.
apps/web
!apps/web/package.json

# Repo furniture.
.git
.github
.pi
*.log
README.md
